-- title:
--   Superadditivity of stabilized channel relative-entropy blocks
-- statement:
--   Let $N,M:L(A)\to L(B)$ be completely positive trace-preserving maps between nonzero finite-dimensional complex Hilbert spaces. Write $B(n)=D(N^{\otimes n}\Vert M^{\otimes n})$ for the stabilized relative entropy in bits, optimized over every unit vector in $A_n\otimes A_n$, with a reference copy of the entire input block. Then, for all $m,n\in\mathbb N$,
--   $$
--   B(m)+B(n)\le B(m+n).
--   $$
--   The inequality is in the extended nonnegative reals and includes infinite divergences. The canonical one-dimensional channel is used at block length zero. Product inputs and tensor regrouping yield this superadditivity, which supports the asymptotic block-limit identity; no finiteness or support-inclusion hypothesis is assumed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/JWang226/Continuity-of-regularized-channel-renyi-divergence/blob/e29274a69978bb499f00497481c6008befb0b84d/QuantumChannelContinuity/RegularizationIdentities.lean#L41-L53

